  "query_preview": "..\n\nThe rest of today through Monday...\n\nWinds will be breezy at times over the western foothills into\nWednesday morning, with gusts generally 30 to 45 mph. As 700 mb \nwinds decrease tonight into Wednesday, surface winds over the \nfoothills will also decrease.\n\nThursday into Friday will see winds increase again, as 700 mb \nwinds increase to 35-50 kts and a favorable pressure gradient for\ngap winds sets up. The chance for strong winds has decreased \nsome, as the timing for the overlap between the favorable pressure\ngradient and the strongest 700 mb winds has shifted a little \nearlier into late Thursday/early Friday and the length of the \noverlap has decreased. Currently, for a gust greater than 60 mph, \nthere is a 45% chance near Harlowton, a 40% chance near \nLivingston, and a 30% chance near Big Timber. Plan ahead as travel\nmay become hazardous Thursday evening into Friday, especially for\nhigh profile vehicles near the foothills. Over the plains, winds \nwill be breezy Friday, with a 40-70% chance of gusts greater than \n30 mph. Along the Dakota border, winds will be strong, with a 40% \nchance of gusts stronger than 50 mph.\n\nIn addition to the winds, the chance for precipitation increases\nas a shortwave, and accompanying push of moisture, moves through \nThursday into early Friday. Currently, the best chance (60-80%) is\nfor snow showers over the Absaroka/Beartooth mountains, with a \nlow chance (10-30%) for light rain showers over the plains. Then, \na stronger shortwave moves through late Friday into Saturday, \nwith another push of moisture, continuing mountain snow and\nallowing a better chance (40-60%) for rain and snow showers\nspreading into the plains. Currently, there is an 80% chance for \nat least 12 inches of snow over the highest peaks of the \nAbsaroka/Beartooth mountains Thursday night through Saturday, and\na 70% chance for at least 6 inches of snow over the Crazy and\nBighorn mountains. Models are currently not bringing much cold \nair with this system, limiting the chance (<20% for half an inch)\nfor accumulating snow farther from the foothills.\n\nUpper level ridging looks to build in Sunday into early next \nweek. There are signs that weak shortwaves may bring low chances \nfor precipitation, mainly to the mountains, and keep temperatures\ncooler.\n\nHighs continue to increase this week from mid 40s Wednesday to 40s\nto low 50s Thursday and Friday. With the stronger wave Saturday,\nhighs will fall into the upper 30s to low 40s and remain there\ninto early next week. Archer",
